"L(3,2,1)-labelings of three classes of 4-valent circulants (https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12574)\nciteturn5academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Authors: Přemysl Holub, Martin Kopřiva ... In this paper, we study $L(3,2,1)$-labelings of three classes of circulant graphs. ... This paper is a continuation of a recent publication of T.\nTitle: L(3,2,1)-labelings of three classes of 4-valent circulants\nAuthors: Přemysl Holub, Martin Kopřiva\nDate: Sun Jan 18 20:36:45 2026\n\nAn $L(3,2,1)$-labeling of a graph $G$ is an assignment $f$ of nonnegative integers to vertices such that $\\vert f(x)-f(y)\\vert > 3-\\mbox{dist}_G(x,y)$ for every pair $x,y$ of vertices of $G$, where $\\mbox{dist}_G(x,y)$ denotes the distance between $x$ and $y$ in $G$. The minimum span (i.e., the difference between the largest and the smallest value) among all $L(3,2,1)$-labelings of $G$ is denoted by $λ_{(3,2,1)}(G)$. In this paper, we study $L(3,2,1)$-labelings of three classes of circulant graphs. Namely, we investigate $λ_{(3,2,1)}$ of $C_n(\\{1,s_2,n-s_2,n-1\\})$, where $s_2\\in\\{3,4,5\\}$. This paper is a continuation of a recent publication of T. Calamoneri who studied the square of cycles, i.e., circulants $C_n(\\{1,2,n-2,n-1\\})$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGraph labelings with restrictive (https://dea.lib.unideb.hu/bitstreams/136f91eb-84cd-40b6-b545-c2fd1e398686/download)\nciteturn5search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; http://wwwusers.di.uniroma1.it/~calamo/PDF-FILES/survey.pdf) ... Chia, ... Kuo, ... Liao, ... 15 (2011), 2439-2457.\nReferences\n[1] W. K. Hale, Frequency assignment: theory and application, Proc. IEEE,\n68 (1980), 1497-1504.\n[2] J. R. Griggs, R. K. Yeh. Labeling graphs with a condition at distance\ntwo. SIAM J. Discrete Math., 5 (1992), pp. 586-595\n[3] T.\nCalamoneri:\nThe\nL(h, k)−labelling\nproblem:\nAn\nup-\ndated\nsurvey\nand\nannotated\nbibliography.\nComput.\nJ.\n54\n(2011),\n1344-1